/*!
\page usd_gltf_page_front UsdGltf: glTF File Format Plugin
\if ( PIXAR_MFB_BUILD )
\mainpage UsdGltf: glTF File Format Plugin
\endif

\section usd_gltf_overview Overview

UsdGltf provides a file format plugin for reading glTF 2.0 assets
(both .gltf and .glb formats) as USD stages. This plugin is based
on Adobe's USD glTF implementation and includes support for the
Khronos Group® glTF™ specification.

\section usd_gltf_features Features

The plugin supports importing glTF 2.0 files with the following features:

- \b Geometry: Meshes with positions, normals, UVs, vertex colors, and skinning data
- \b Materials: Support for UsdPreviewSurface and material extensions
- \b Textures: Image references and embedded textures
- \b Transforms: Node hierarchies with transformations
- \b Animation: Skeletal animations and transform animations
- \b Cameras: Perspective and orthographic cameras
- \b Lights: Support for KHR_lights_punctual extension

\subsection usd_gltf_extensions glTF Extensions

The plugin supports various glTF extensions including:
- KHR_materials_specular
- KHR_materials_anisotropy
- KHR_materials_clearcoat
- KHR_draco_mesh_compression (when Draco support is enabled)
- And others

\section usd_gltf_usage Usage

Once the plugin is built and installed, glTF files can be opened
directly with USD tools:

\code
# Open a glTF file
usdcat model.gltf

# View a glTF file
usdview model.glb

# Reference a glTF file in a USD stage
from pxr import Usd
stage = Usd.Stage.Open("model.gltf")
\endcode

\subsection usd_gltf_file_format_args File Format Arguments

The plugin supports several file format arguments for customization:

- \c assetsPath - Alternative path to store imported assets
- \c animationTracks - Enable importing multiple animation tracks (default: false)

Example usage with file format arguments:

\code
stage = Usd.Stage.Open("model.gltf:SDF_FORMAT_ARGS:animationTracks=true")
\endcode

\section usd_gltf_package_resolver Package Resolution

The plugin includes a package resolver (GltfResolver) that enables
glTF files to be treated as packages, allowing referenced assets
(textures, binary data) to be properly resolved whether they are
embedded or external.

\section usd_gltf_limitations Limitations

- The plugin provides read-only support (import only)
- Some advanced glTF features may have limited support
- Export functionality is not currently implemented

\section usd_gltf_dependencies Dependencies

- \b TinyGLTF - Required for glTF parsing (automatically downloaded)
- \b Draco - Optional for compressed mesh support (uses existing USD Draco if available)

\section usd_gltf_build Building

The plugin is built as part of USD when the \c PXR_BUILD_GLTF_PLUGIN option is enabled:

\code
cmake -DPXR_BUILD_GLTF_PLUGIN=ON ...
\endcode

For Draco compression support, also enable:

\code
cmake -DPXR_BUILD_GLTF_PLUGIN=ON -DPXR_BUILD_DRACO_PLUGIN=ON ...
\endcode

\section usd_gltf_credits Credits

This plugin is based on Adobe's USD File Format Plugins project:
https://github.com/adobe/USD-Fileformat-plugins
*/
